Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Assertion (A):</strong></span></td><td>Boric acid is a weak acid</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason (R):</strong></td><td>Boric acid is not able to release <span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{H^+}\)</span> ion on its own. It receives <span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{OH^-}\)</span> ion from water and releases <span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{H^+}\)</span> ion.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong></span> and <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> are correct and <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> is the correct explanation of <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong></span>.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong></span> and <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> are correct but <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> is NOT the correct explanation of <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong>.</span></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong></span> is correct but <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> is not correct</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(A)</strong></span> is not correct but <span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>(R)</strong></span> is correct</td></tr></tbody></table>
